config VIDEO_IMX219_OOT
	bool "Sony IMX219 (out-of-tree fork)"
	select I2C
	depends on DT_HAS_SONY_IMX219_ENABLED
	help
	  Use this repository's fork of the IMX219 driver instead of Zephyr's
	  in-tree drivers/video/imx219.c, to correct the sensor's PLL programming
	  against Raspberry Pi's kernel driver.

	  Both bind the "sony,imx219" compatible, so set CONFIG_VIDEO_IMX219=n
	  when enabling this, or the build will define the same device twice.

config VIDEO_OV5647
	bool "OmniVision OV5647 (Raspberry Pi Camera Module v1)"
	default y
	select I2C
	depends on DT_HAS_OVTI_OV5647_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable the OV5647 MIPI CSI-2 image sensor driver. Zephyr has no in-tree
	  OV5647 driver, so unlike the IMX219 above there is no symbol to turn off
	  alongside this one.

	  Implements the 800x640 and 800x800 RAW8 50 fps modes, ported from
	  Espressif's esp_cam_sensor component and both verified streaming on
	  hardware. Frames are Bayer GBRG - nothing in Zephyr's ESP32-P4 CSI path
	  demosaics them, so an application gets raw Bayer and must debayer itself.

	  RAW10 is not offered: it needs the ESP32-P4 ISP's bypass path, which does
	  not deliver complete frames (see the comment in ov5647.c).

config VIDEO_ESP32_CSI
	bool "ESP32-P4 MIPI CSI-2 camera receiver"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_ESPRESSIF_ESP32P4_MIPI_CSI_ENABLED
	depends on SOC_SERIES_ESP32P4
	help
	  Enable the ESP32-P4 MIPI CSI-2 receiver video-capture driver. It drives
	  the CSI D-PHY, host and bridge, and a DW-GDMA channel that streams frames
	  from a downstream CSI-2 image sensor (e.g. Sony IMX219) into memory.
	  Uses the video subsystem log level (CONFIG_VIDEO_LOG_LEVEL).

config VIDEO_ARDUCAM_PIVARIETY
	bool "Arducam Pivariety camera"
	default y
	select I2C
	depends on DT_HAS_ARDUCAM_PIVARIETY_ENABLED
	help
	  Enable the Arducam Pivariety camera driver. Pivariety modules carry an
	  on-board MCU that describes the module's formats, resolutions and
	  controls over I2C, so this one driver serves every camera in the family
	  (including the Arducam ToF depth camera) without per-sensor register
	  tables.

	  Frames are delivered raw. Any depth or Bayer processing is the
	  application's problem.

config VIDEO_ARDUCAM_PIVARIETY_MAX_FORMATS
	int "Maximum enumerated (format, resolution) pairs"
	default 16
	depends on VIDEO_ARDUCAM_PIVARIETY
	help
	  Upper bound on the video_format_cap array the driver builds at init.
	  One entry is needed per (pixel format, resolution) pair, not per pixel
	  format, since each entry carries its own width/height bounds.

	  A module reporting more pairs than this is truncated with a warning
	  rather than rejected: a partially usable camera beats a dead one.
